<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-12.00%" pitch="-3.00%">
      In prison, Joseph met two servants of Pharaoh.<break time="500ms"/>
      The chief cupbearer and the chief baker.<break time="500ms"/>
      Each one dreamed in the night and woke troubled by what had been seen.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Joseph listened carefully.<break time="500ms"/>
      He said that interpretations belong to God.<break time="500ms"/>
      Then he spoke what the dreams meant.<break time="1800ms"/>

      The meanings came to pass just as he had said.<break time="500ms"/>
      And Joseph asked the cupbearer to remember him when he returned to Pharaoh's house.<break time="1000ms"/>
      A simple request.<break time="500ms"/>
      Please do not leave me here forgotten.<break time="1800ms"/>

      But the cupbearer did forget him.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not for a day only.<break time="500ms"/>
      For two full years.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Time moved slowly in that place.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Morning after morning, the same walls would have met his eyes.<break time="500ms"/>
      Yet the Lord had not misplaced him there.<break time="1800ms"/>

      This may be the quietest part of Joseph's story.<break time="500ms"/>
      No robe.<break time="500ms"/>
      No field.<break time="500ms"/>
      No sudden rescue.<break time="500ms"/>
      Only waiting that seemed to stretch on and on.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Forgotten by people does not mean forgotten by God.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The hidden years are still years held by Him.<break time="1000ms"/>
      You are not forgotten in waiting.<break time="1800ms"/>
      You can rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
